.rm 65
.bd
SUBROUTINE
.in +5
.br
.bd
strrchr
- find last occurrence of a character
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
C
.in +5
.br
.bd 3
char *strrchr(s, c)
char *s;
char c;
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
FUNCTION
.in +5
.br
strrchr returns a pointer to the last occurrence of the
character c in the string s.  The terminating null is
considered part of the string, so strrchr(s, '\0') returns a
pointer to the terminator.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
RETURNS
.in +5
.br
a pointer to c in s, or 0 if c does not appear.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
NOTES
.in +5
.br
rindex is the pre-ANSI name for strrchr; the two are the same
routine.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
ALSO READ
.in +5
.br
strchr (3), strlen (3)
